[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186157276 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-226b9b94-926b-577f-834a-35ff659d1159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-226b9b94-926b-577f-834a-35ff659d1159" :question/id #uuid "226b9b94-926b-577f-834a-35ff659d1159" :question/math-academy-id "q-102338" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 4+(-15)\\cdot 3}{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-45}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{25} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{2}=15\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3231d9e1-5db0-532b-9d06-68eafedeb402"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3231d9e1-5db0-532b-9d06-68eafedeb402" :answer-field/id #uuid "3231d9e1-5db0-532b-9d06-68eafedeb402" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-354f21b2-96ab-5d34-8629-17b1cd8d23d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f270c863-ecf9-5d37-bac9-47ebceb975b3" "answer-354f21b2-96ab-5d34-8629-17b1cd8d23d3" "answer-c3ccdf0e-7384-5c78-bdab-6715b3b614a5" "answer-800e78fd-bc77-5f21-8b03-8b51fc29c534" "answer-5ee3cf3b-86e3-5e57-83f5-b5451cd4c7b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f270c863-ecf9-5d37-b